course: dictionary
lesson: 947
title: Blood: the red liquid and the family word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blood is a red liquid. Your heart pumps it through tubes called blood vessels, so it reaches every part of your body. «Blood is always red, bright red with oxygen and dark red without, even though veins look blue through your skin.» The veins look blue because of your skin, not because the blood is blue.
explain: Blood has important jobs. It carries oxygen and food to every part of the body and takes waste away. Red blood cells carry oxygen, white blood cells fight germs, and platelets help a cut stop bleeding.
explain: Blood also has a second meaning: family. «They are related by blood» means the people share the same ancestors. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Is the sentence about a heart and tubes, or about people and families?
explain: Blood is uncountable, so you say some blood, not a blood. Bloody and bloodless are related words: bloody means covered in blood, and bloodless means without blood or without much colour.
fact: Blood is a liquid that the heart pumps around the body through blood vessels.
fact: «An African elephant's two huge ears are like radiators full of blood vessels, so flapping them cools the blood.»
fact: «A bump on the head swells because the scalp has many blood vessels that leak under the skin; the size of the bump does not show how serious the injury is.»
fact: In first aid, press on a bleeding cut with a clean cloth and tell an adult. Do not touch other people's blood without gloves.
fact: Blood can mean the red liquid in your body, or family and ancestors, as in «They are related by blood».
exercise: What do red blood cells carry around the body? | Water only | Heat | *Oxygen | Germs
exercise: Which part of blood helps a cut stop bleeding? | Red blood cells | White blood cells | Lungs | *Platelets
exercise: What should you do with a bleeding cut? | Put it in the sun | Touch the blood with bare hands to clean it | *Press on it with a clean cloth and tell an adult | Leave it and walk away
test: What does blood mean in «They are related by blood»? | A red liquid pumped by the heart | Bright red paint | A cut on the skin | *Family or ancestors
test: Why does a bump on the head swell? | *Because the scalp has many blood vessels that leak under the skin | Because the bump is always flat | Because the head is hot | Because the bone is broken
exam: Which sentence uses blood to mean family? | «The heart pumps blood through the body.» | «The elephant's ears are full of blood vessels.» | *«They are related by blood.» | «Blood is always red.»
